### `findFileMarker` (scanning for the marker)
This function iterates through the data looking for file markers:

```go
func findFileMarker(data []byte) (before []byte, name string, after []byte) {
    var i int
    for {
        // Check current position for marker using isMarker
        if name, after = isMarker(data[i:]); name != "" {
            return data[:i], name, after
        }
        // If no marker, look for next line start
        j := bytes.Index(data[i:], newlineMarker)
        if j < 0 {
            return fixNL(data), "", nil
        }
        i += j + 1 // move to start of next line
    }
}
```

### `Parse` (main entry point)
```go
func Parse(data []byte) *Archive {
    a := new(Archive)
    var name string
    // First, extract the initial comment if present
    a.Comment, name, data = findFileMarker(data)
    for name != "" {
        // Each iteration finds the next file marker
        f := File{name, nil}
        f.Data, name, data = findFileMarker(data)
        a.Files = append(a.Files, f)
    }
    return a
}
```

## Summary

